---
// SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Numen Games S.L.
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//
// /automation — what an agent may do without asking, level by level.
//
// WHY THIS PAGE EXISTS
// An agent asks its operator for permission many times a session, and each
// request arrives as a line of shell: "git clone --depth 50 …" flagged as "URL
// points to IP address 0.0.0.50". The operator did not write the shell and is
// asked to answer for it. He asked for the permissions an agent needs here to
// be drawn somewhere, in his words: what each one is, what it implies, and
// at which level of automation it is granted alone.
//
// THIS PAGE STATES NOTHING OF ITS OWN. It arranges what the archive already
// says — who may change what, the approval protocol, the engineering
// protocol, each agent's OPERATOR.md, the transition regime — into the five
// levels of the ISO/IEC 22989 automation scale, and grades every permission
// at each. The data is web/src/lib/automation-levels.ts; each agent's level
// is read from the `automation_level:` header of its OPERATOR.md; a test
// holds both to shape. The instrument is the home's astrolabe: five rings from the least
// automated at the centre to the most at the rim, and a dotted line beyond
// the rim for the floor — what no level grants alone.
//
// Sibling of /binding: that page says which rules bind today; this one says
// what an agent may do today under them.
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import DocToolbar from "@/components/DocToolbar.astro";
import { repoFileUrl } from "@/lib/build-info";
import { LEVELS, PERMISSIONS, agentMarks, SOURCES, GRADE_LABEL, AUTOMATION_SOURCES } from "@/lib/automation-levels";
import type { Grade } from "@/lib/automation-levels";

const CX = 360, CY = 360;
const P = (r: number, a: number) => { const t = ((a - 90) * Math.PI) / 180; return [CX + r * Math.cos(t), CY + r * Math.sin(t)]; };
const RR: [number, number][] = [[0, 70], [76, 124], [130, 178], [184, 232], [238, 286]];
const disc = (r: number) => `M${CX - r},${CY}a${r},${r} 0 1,0 ${2 * r},0a${r},${r} 0 1,0 ${-2 * r},0Z`;
const ringPath = (r0: number, r1: number) => (r0 === 0 ? disc(r1) : `${disc(r1)} ${disc(r0)}`);
const textArc = (rm: number) => { const [x0, y0] = P(rm, -88), [x1, y1] = P(rm, 88); return `M${x0},${y0}A${rm},${rm} 0 0,1 ${x1},${y1}`; };
const ticks = Array.from({ length: 72 }, (_, i) => i * 5).map((a) => {
  const L = a % 45 === 0; const [x0, y0] = P(288, a), [x1, y1] = P(L ? 302 : a % 15 === 0 ? 296 : 292, a);
  return { x0, y0, x1, y1, L };
});
const marks = agentMarks().map((m) => {
  const r = RR[m.level]; const rm = m.level === 0 ? 40 : (r[0] + r[1]) / 2;
  const [x, y] = P(rm, m.angle); const [lx, ly] = P(rm + 16, m.angle);
  return { ...m, x, y, lx, ly, end: m.angle > 180 };
});
const today = LEVELS.find((l) => l.today)!;
const grade = (g: Grade) => `pill ${g}`;
---

<Layout
  title="What an agent may do without asking — numinia-archive"
  description="The permissions an agent needs to operate here, in the approver's words, graded at five levels of automation. Nothing new: the rules the archive already holds, arranged for the person who says yes."
  canonicalPath="/automation"
>
  <section class="auto mx-auto max-w-[1280px] px-6 pb-24 pt-10">
    <div class="stage">
      <div class="ctx" aria-live="polite">
        <div class="et">Beside <a href="/binding">what binds today</a></div>
        <h1>What an agent may do without asking</h1>
        <p>Every permission an agent asks for arrives as a line of shell. This view puts it in the approver's words: which permissions exist, what each implies, and which are granted alone at each level of automation. It states nothing of its own: it reads each agent's operator file, the permission register and the approval protocol.</p>
        <div class="qa">
          <div class="depth" role="tablist" aria-label="Level">
            {LEVELS.map((l) => <button type="button" role="tab" data-l={l.id} aria-selected={l.today ? "true" : "false"}><span></span><i>{l.name}</i></button>)}
          </div>
          {LEVELS.map((l) => (
            <div class="lv" data-l={l.id} hidden={!l.today}>
              <h2>{l.name}{l.today && <span class="today">Ursa is here</span>}</h2>
              <p>{l.line}</p>
              <div class="kv"><b>You</b><span>{l.you}</span><b>Where you approve</b><span>{l.where}</span><b>The agent does alone</b><span>{l.alone}</span><b>It asks</b><span>{l.asks}</span></div>
              <p class="classic">Equivalent: {l.equiv}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <div class="qa">
          <h2>What no level grants alone</h2>
          <p>Four permissions are floor across the whole scale: the repository's settings, the domains, money, and the agent's own identity. The dotted line around the circle is that floor. Beyond it, a system that sets its own goals: out of the map by design.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mapcol">
        <div class="lenses"><span class="et">Show</span><button type="button" class="ctl on" data-view="levels">The levels</button><button type="button" class="ctl" data-view="agents">Where each agent is</button></div>
        <svg class="astro" viewBox="-20 -20 760 760" role="group" aria-label="The five levels of automation">
          <defs>
            {RR.map((r, i) => <path id={`t-${i}`} d={textArc((r[0] + r[1]) / 2)} />)}
            <path id="t-floor" d={textArc(322)} />
          </defs>
          <circle class="rim" cx={CX} cy={CY} r="288" />
          {ticks.map((t) => <line class:list={["tick", t.L && "l"]} x1={t.x0} y1={t.y0} x2={t.x1} y2={t.y1} />)}
          {LEVELS.map((l, i) => (
            <g class:list={["ring", l.today && "sel"]} data-l={l.id} tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label={l.name} aria-pressed={l.today ? "true" : "false"} data-tip={`${l.name}|${l.you}`}>
              <path class="f" d={ringPath(RR[i][0], RR[i][1])} fill-rule="evenodd" />
              {i === 0
                ? <><text class="core-t" x={CX} y={CY + 2}>{l.name}</text><text class="core-s" x={CX} y={CY + 20}>the person does</text></>
                : <text class="w"><textPath href={`#t-${i}`} startOffset="50%" text-anchor="middle">{l.name}</textPath></text>}
            </g>
          ))}
          <circle class="floor-ring" cx={CX} cy={CY} r="312" />
          <text class="floor-l"><textPath href="#t-floor" startOffset="50%" text-anchor="middle">the floor · what no level grants alone</textPath></text>
          <g class="marks" hidden>
            {marks.map((m) => (
              <g data-tip={`${m.name}|${LEVELS[m.level].name} · ${m.note}`}>
                <circle class:list={["agent-dot", m.ghost && "ghost"]} cx={m.x} cy={m.y} r="5" />
                <text class="agent-l" x={m.lx} y={m.ly + 3} text-anchor={m.end ? "end" : "start"}>{m.name}</text>
              </g>
            ))}
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sec">The permissions, level by level</h2>
    <p class="lede">A permission is always described the same way: what it is, what it lets the agent do, what could go wrong, whether it can be undone, and who grants it today. Open a row to read it; pick a column to change level.</p>
    <div class="legend"><span class="pill alone">alone</span><span>does it without asking</span><span class="pill ask">asks</span><span>stops and waits for a yes</span><span class="pill never">never</span><span>no level grants it alone</span></div>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="matrix">
        <thead><tr><th></th><th>Permission</th>{LEVELS.map((l) => <th class:list={["lvl", l.today && "active"]} data-l={l.id}><button type="button" data-l={l.id}>{l.name}</button></th>)}<th>Undone</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {PERMISSIONS.map((p) => (
            <>
              <tr class="perm" data-n={p.n}>
                <td class="n">{String(p.n).padStart(2, "0")}</td>
                <td><button type="button" class="row-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls={`d-${p.n}`}>{p.name}</button></td>
                {p.levels.map((g, i) => <td class:list={["lvl", LEVELS[i].today && "active"]} data-l={i}><span class={grade(g)}>{GRADE_LABEL[g]}</span></td>)}
                <td class="undo">{p.undo}</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="detail" id={`d-${p.n}`} hidden>
                <td colspan="8">
                  <div class="grid"><div><b>What it lets it do</b>{p.lets}</div><div><b>What could go wrong</b>{p.wrong}</div><div><b>Undone</b>{p.undo}</div><div><b>Who grants it today</b>{p.who}</div><div><b>Risk it bounds</b>{p.risk}</div></div>
                  {p.floor && <div class="floor"><b>Floor.</b> {p.floor}</div>}
                  <div class="why">{p.levels.map((g, i) => <span data-l={i} hidden={!LEVELS[i].today}>At <b>{LEVELS[i].name}</b>: {g === "alone" ? "it does it alone, without notice; it stays in the session's record." : g === "ask" ? "it stops, explains it in your words and waits for your go." : "it does not do it. If it needs it, it asks you as a decision of yours, never as a permission."}</span>)}</div>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sec">How a request reads</h2>
    <p class="lede">The approval protocol says this; here it is only shown. The same request, written twice. Whatever the level, the question is asked the same way: what I am about to do, what could go wrong, whether it can be undone. The shell goes underneath, for whoever wants to read it.</p>
    <div class="dialogs">
      <div class="dlg">
        <div class="et">Today</div>
        <pre>Command required approval (Security scan — [MEDIUM] URL uses raw IP address: URL points to IP address 0.0.0.50 instead of a domain name; [MEDIUM] Schemeless URL in sink context: URL without explicit scheme passed to a command that downloads/executes content)

cd …/scratch && git clone -q --depth 50 https://github.com/numengames/numinia-archive.git</pre>
        <div class="btns"><span class="btn">Approve</span><span class="btn">Deny</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="dlg new">
        <div class="et">Proposed</div>
        <pre><b>I am about to copy the archive (numinia.org) to my desk.</b>
Permissions: <span class="pill alone">read the repositories</span> <span class="pill alone">write on my desk</span>
What could go wrong: nothing outside my folder; about 40 MB of disk.
Undone: yes, it is deleted.
At your level today (<b>{today.name}</b>) this asks; at Conditional it would go alone.<span class="cmd">git clone --depth 50 https://github.com/numengames/numinia-archive.git</span></pre>
        <div class="btns"><span class="btn enter">Go ahead</span><span class="btn">Not this time</span><span class="btn stop">Stop and explain</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sec">Where this comes from</h2>
    <ul class="sources">
      {SOURCES.map((s) => <li>{s.href ? <a href={s.href}>{s.text}</a> : s.text}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <div class="mt-10">
      <DocToolbar
        mdUrl="/automation.md"
        filename="automation.md"
        repoUrl={repoFileUrl(AUTOMATION_SOURCES[0]) ?? "https://github.com/numengames/numinia-archive/blob/main/standards/STD-017-who-may-change-what.md"}
        lang="en"
      />
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="tip" id="tip" role="tooltip"></div>
</Layout>

<style is:global>
  .auto { --t1: rgb(var(--text)); --t2: rgb(var(--text-muted)); --t3: rgb(var(--text-dim)); --lf: rgb(var(--border)); --int: rgb(var(--teal)); --amb: rgb(var(--ambar)); }
